<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "5B">
<servcat sctnbr = "05" scnbr = "02">
<configtype typenbr = "0">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A5206017" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "02" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Manual Transaxle Assembly Disassembly and Reassembly
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206012">Manual Transaxle Unit Dismounting and Remounting</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206016">Manual Transaxle Assembly Components</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A5206017001">
<title>
Disassembly
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove back up light switch. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206007"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove gear shift and select shaft assembly. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206014"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove transaxle case bolts.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove transaxle left side case (1) from right case using special tool.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L5B010">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09912-34510">
09912–34510
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IAY301520026.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "55.580mm" ver = "01" gw = "165" gh = "141"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove reverse gear shift lever bolts (1) and reverse gear shift lever (2).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I5RW0B520024.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "70.640mm" ver = "01" gw = "168" gh = "184"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Tapping input shaft end with plastic hammer, push it out as assembly from case a little, and then remove input shaft assembly (1), countershaft assembly (2), high speed gear shift shaft (3), low speed gear shift shaft (4), 5th &#38; 6th gear shift shaft (5), reverse gear shift shaft (6), reverse idler gear assembly (7) and revers gear shift fork shaft.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I5RW0B520025.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "59.208mm" ver = "01" gw = "159" gh = "151"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove differential assembly from transaxle right case.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A5206017002">
<title>
Reassembly
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206018">Transaxle Right Case Disassembly and Reassembly</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206019">Transaxle Left Case Disassembly and Reassembly</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206021">Input Shaft Disassembly and Reassembly</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206024">Countershaft Disassembly and Reassembly</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206026">Reverse Idler Gear Assembly Components</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206031">Differential Disassembly and Reassembly</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5206029">Gear Shift Shaft and Fork Inspection</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Select input shaft shim, countershaft shim and reverse idler gear shim as follows.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Measure depth of transaxle left case (1) i.e., “a” for input shaft assembly, “e” for countershaft assembly and “i” for reverse idler gear assembly.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Measure depth of right case (2) i.e., “b” for input shaft assembly, “f” for countershaft assembly and “j” for reverse idler gear assembly.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Measure distance “c” of input shaft assembly (3) and “k” of reverse idler gear assembly (4).
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Measure distance “g” of countershaft assembly (5) according to the following procedure.
</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>
Remove countershaft right bearing outer race from transaxle right case. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206018"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>
Remove countershaft left bearing outer race from transaxle left case. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206019"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>
Set countershaft bearing outer races to countershaft.
</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>
Keep pressing countershaft bearing outer race with 34 N (3.5 kgf, 7.6 lbf) and turn countershaft assembly 10 times or more.
</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>
Measure distance “g” of countershaft assembly.
</ptxt>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Calculate the clearance of “d” for input shaft, “h” for countershaft and “l” for reverse idler by the following formulas.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
Clearance “d” = depth “a” + depth “b” – distance “c”
</emph>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
Clearance “h” = depth “e” + depth “f” – distance “g”
</emph>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
<emph etype = "bold">
Clearance “l” = depth “i” + depth “j” – distance “k”
</emph>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IHSB0A523022.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "166.158mm" ver = "01" gw = "207" gh = "454"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Select shim closest to clearance “d”, “h” and “l” from the following available sizes.
</ptxt>
