<s1>
<ptxt>
Install countershaft right bearing outer race to transaxle right case. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206018"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install countershaft shim and countershaft left bearing outer race to transaxle left case. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5206019"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply transaxle oil to differential side bearings.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install differential assembly into transaxle right case.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply transaxle oil to input shaft right bearing, countershaft left bearing and right bearing.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Join input shaft assembly (5), countershaft assembly (4), low speed gear shift shaft (2), high speed gear shift shaft (3), 5th &#38; 6th gear shift shaft (6), reverse gear shift shaft (7), reverse idler gear assembly (8) and reverse gear shift fork shaft all together, and then install them into transaxle right case (1) so as not to damage oil seal by input shaft spline.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Input shaft right bearing on shaft can be installed into transaxle right case by tapping shaft with plastic hammer.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that countershaft is engaged with final gear while installing.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I5RW0B520026.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "64.257mm" ver = "01" gw = "161" gh = "166"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply grease to input shaft shim (1).
</ptxt>
<materials>
<materialitem name = "ECSTAR Grease A" id = "M5B006" uid = "1545785286">
<m-part>
“A”
</m-part>
<m-desc>
Grease
</m-desc>
<m-number>
99000–25480
</m-number>
<m-name>
ECSTAR Grease A
</m-name>
</materialitem>
</materials>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install input shaft shim and reverse idler gear shim (2).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IHSB0P522024.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "66.583mm" ver = "02" gw = "175" gh = "200"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install reverse gear shift lever (1) and then tighten new reverse gear shift lever bolts (2) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
The reverse gear shift lever bolts are pre-coated with adhesive. If these bolts are reused, they may work loose.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Replace the reverse gear shift lever bolts with new ones whenever they are removed.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T5B013">
<t-part>
Reverse gear shift lever bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
23
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
2.3
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
17.0
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IAY301520028.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "72.931mm" ver = "01" gw = "169" gh = "190"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean mating surfaces of both right and left cases, and apply sealant to transaxle right case (1) as shown in figure. Diameter of applied sealant is 1.5 mm (0.059 in.).
</ptxt>
<materials>
<materialitem name = "SUZUKI Bond No.1217G" id = "M5B007" uid = "-491504098">
<m-part>
“A”
</m-part>
<m-desc>
Sealant
</m-desc>
<m-number>
99000–31260
</m-number>
<m-name>
SUZUKI Bond No.1217G
</m-name>
</materialitem>
</materials>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Mate it with transaxle left case (2).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Tighten transaxle case bolts (3) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T5B014">
<t-part>
Transaxle case bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
23
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
2.3
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
17.0
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I5RW0B520030.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "90.328mm" ver = "01" gw = "146" gh = "239"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install back up light switch. 
